# Isolating, and it has to say so: without this file Gradle assumes the worst of any processor on
# the annotation path and recompiles every source file in the project on every change — in every
# build that adds this module. That cost is paid by adopters, not by this repository, which is
# what makes it worth a line of configuration.
#
# The contract Gradle asks for is that every decision comes from the annotated element and what is
# reachable from it, and that each generated file names exactly one originating element. All four
# checks qualify: the custom masker check reads the class the annotation names, the rebuild check
# reads the owning class and its superclass chain, and the justification and partial-reveal checks
# read attributes of the annotation itself. Nothing consults another source file in the round, and
# nothing is generated at all — there is no aggregate output an incremental round could rewrite
# with half of it missing.
ch.raph.datamask.processor.PiiProcessor,ISOLATING
